"number of bands in the bar (and hence the number of values required to "
"follow the x,y coordinate pair in the input). Here, +i means we must "
"accumulate the bar values from the increments dy or dx, while +v means we "
"get the complete values relative to base. Normally, the bands are plotted as "
"sections of a final single bar. Use +s to instead split the bar into ny or "
"nx side-by-side, individual and thinner bars. Multi-band bars require "
"cmap=True with one color per band.\">"
